  "description_short": "Hearty home-style meals and fresh farmstall produce in the heart of Storms River village.",
  "description_long": "Tucked along Gammasi Street in Storms River village, Taste Restaurant and Farmstall offers honest country cooking that fuels adventures in the Tsitsikamma. The menu delivers generous portions of home-style favourites—think proper breakfast plates, toasted sandwiches, and daily specials that change with what's fresh. The attached farmstall stocks local produce, preserves, and supplies for self-caterers exploring the area.\n\nThe relaxed atmosphere suits families stopping between hikes and travellers needing a proper meal before tackling the passes. Service is straightforward and friendly, with locals often popping in for their regular orders. It's the kind of place where you'll find hikers comparing trail notes over coffee and residents catching up over lunch.\n\nThe location makes it an easy stop whether you're heading to the Bloukrans Bridge, exploring the forest trails, or just passing through this gateway to the Tsitsikamma. Prices are kept honest for a village that sees plenty of tourists, and portions ensure you won't leave hungry before your next adventure.",
